From: kuf-cod-recomp
Subject: [PATCH] content: transactional save packages, content_root, fatal CLI errors

Saves (Xbox 360 content packages) were host directories written in place, and CREATE_ALWAYS deleted an
existing package before the new one existed: a crash or kill while the game saved could leave a half-written
save or none. Guest writes now go to a staging copy that replaces the package atomically
(renameat2 RENAME_EXCHANGE, after fsync) on XamContentClose/XamContentFlush; CREATE_ALWAYS and
TRUNCATE_EXISTING keep the old package until the replacement is committed. A manifest (size and SHA-256
per file) is committed with each package and verified on open (content_damaged=refuse|load). Leftovers of
an interrupted session are recovered on first access and never applied. Runtime files (.rex-*) are hidden
from the guest. content_root puts saves in their own directory. content_test_kill (tests only) kills the
process at a chosen commit stage. Every content call is logged with a [content] prefix.

A CLI parse error used to apply none of the options and run on with defaults (paths included); it now
exits with status 2 (help-style exits unchanged).

